1
00:00:00,063 --> 00:00:02,323
A time we cannot return to.

2
00:00:04,556 --> 00:00:07,896
We used to roam between neighbourhoods.

3
00:00:07,956 --> 00:00:09,916
Our neighbourhood was about this big.

4
00:00:09,956 --> 00:00:13,476
We went to the same primary school,

5
00:00:13,536 --> 00:00:16,236
and we all lived nearby.

6
00:00:16,276 --> 00:00:20,536
So we would roam quite far when we went out to play.

7
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:27,076
We would visit other neighbourhoods just to play in the lifts.

8
00:00:29,376 --> 00:00:32,076
There was a well, too. A very deep well.

9
00:00:32,136 --> 00:00:35,716
We dropped stones in and listened for the sound,

10
00:00:35,776 --> 00:00:37,016
to work out how deep it was.

11
00:00:37,076 --> 00:00:39,856
It felt as though something mysterious was down there.

12
00:00:39,896 --> 00:00:42,016
Me too. Like a tunnel underground.

13
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:45,520
I went back recently and visited places from my childhood.

14
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,520
Let me show you.

15
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:50,590
This is the place in my earliest memory.

16
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:52,230
It used to be a square.

17
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:55,190
My grandad used to bring me here to buy things.

18
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,710
That is my earliest memory.

19
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:00,290
Your earliest memory.

20
00:01:01,224 --> 00:01:02,384
This was a little shop.

21
00:01:02,824 --> 00:01:05,244
I used to hang out there as a kid.

22
00:01:05,304 --> 00:01:06,504
Nobody at home kept tabs on me.

23
00:01:06,544 --> 00:01:09,144
The old lady who ran it was so kind to me.

24
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:12,270
I lived here in primary school. Seven or eight years later,

25
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:14,690
I used to skip classes in high school.

26
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:16,870
One day I skipped class and went back to see her.

27
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:18,470
I bought a few things.

28
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:20,190
I said, “Do you remember me?”

29
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:22,750
She thought about it, but could not place me.

30
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:25,370
Then suddenly: “You are Zhuangzhuang!”

31
00:01:25,410 --> 00:01:25,870
Wow.

32
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:28,850
She recognised me. I was so moved.

33
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:30,930
She would not take my money, either.

34
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:32,350
I should have paid first.

35
00:01:32,739 --> 00:01:36,879
What struck me was walking in: it was just as it had been.

36
00:01:36,919 --> 00:01:39,039
Even she looked just the same as seven or eight years before.

37
00:01:39,299 --> 00:01:40,539
It was almost too much for me.

38
00:01:40,579 --> 00:01:42,639
After that, I was afraid to go and see her.

39
00:01:42,679 --> 00:01:46,259
I thought she would give me things again, so I stayed away.

40
00:01:46,339 --> 00:01:47,779
You could bring her something first.

41
00:01:47,819 --> 00:01:48,439
That is true.

42
00:01:49,021 --> 00:01:51,241
In high school, I would skip class and watch the sunset here.

43
00:01:51,661 --> 00:01:52,301
Beautiful.

44
00:01:52,361 --> 00:01:53,861
I watched the sunset here every day.

45
00:01:53,901 --> 00:01:54,221
Beautiful.

46
00:01:54,731 --> 00:01:57,191
But by making a film, you can go back once more.

47
00:01:57,711 --> 00:01:59,911
You cannot live back then forever,

48
00:01:59,971 --> 00:02:01,671
or keep looking back forever.

49
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:05,271
We have lovely friends here now, too. People to play with.

